llegations and their governance procedures for dealing with such allegations; (b) the actions taken by the RBA once it was made aware of these allegations and whether the actions were appropriate and timely in the circumstances; (c) the involvement of Austrade in the activities of Securency International Ltd and Note Printing Australia; (d) Austrade's knowledge of the allegations, including dates, and their actions thereto; (e) the role of the Australian Securities and Investments Commission (ASIC) in investigating these allegations, and whether ASIC acted in a timely manner in relation to these matters; and (f) any other related matters. Mark Bishop The question before the chair is that notice of motion No. 1, moved in the names of Senator Milne and Senator Xenophon, be agreed to.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-242","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2012-09-12/4"}
